    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 549 of 2005",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7668\n\nSPONSOR: SEWARD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend chapter 549 of the laws of 2005 amend-\ning the tax law relating to authorizing the county of Herkimer to impose\na county recording tax on obligation secured by a mortgage on real prop-\nerty, in relation to the expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend provisions authorizing Herkimer County to impose an additional\nmortgage recording tax of twenty-five cents for each one hundred dollars\nof debt until December 1, 2020.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one - amends section 2 of chapter 549 of the laws of 2005 to\nauthorize Herkimer County to enact a mortgage recording tax of twenty-\nfive cents for each one hundred dollars of debt until December 1, 2020.\n\nSection two - provides the effective date.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe current authorization expires on December 1, 2018.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Herkimer County Legislature has requested the introduction of this\nlegislation by local resolution.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill. Formerly S. 6807 of 2016.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
